  "review": {
    "review": "The full public death message confirms a skeleton killed the hero during the final zap. The actionable initiating defect in the last escape attempt precedes that shot: decision 3754 (selection line 10794) chooses door 425 through squares already adjacent to observed skeleton 424. The escape selector pools exposure, so leaving guard 647 offsets entering the different skeleton’s reach. The accepted move reaches 613 with 62 HP; at decision 3755 the route is unreachable and sustained combat follows. Isolated public-scene and reduced-fixture probes reproduce the original route without claiming recovered runtime memory. The proposed correction checks each observed non-DM attacker separately for new and committed door flights. The new regression fails twice as expected on original code and passes all four tests after the fix; the full suite passes 2,048 tests with four skipped. This prevents the evidenced route admission, not proof of a safe replacement or survival. Pre-death unidentified items were not assigned post-death identities.",
    "learnings": "Do not treat escaping one attacker as permission to approach another along a committed escape route. Recheck opposing observed threats before starting or continuing doorway flight. Rejecting an obstructed route does not establish a safe alternative."
